SUSPECTED BUG: Seal returns errors.Join(werr, serr, f.Close()) with three stdlib-sized
operands ((*os.File).Write: 22 values, Stat: 17, Close: 8; see seal_write_call_site).
Expected: under one errors.Join link, the union of the three operand sets, in particular
every origin of seal_write_call_site, e.g. io.ErrUnexpectedEOF, io.ErrShortWrite and
internal/poll.ErrDeadlineExceeded under *fs.PathError.Unwrap; or, if a size cap is hit,
an explicit Unresolved(fixpoint-limit) entry. Actual: 27 entries and NO
Unresolved(fixpoint-limit); six Write origins are silently missing (io.ErrUnexpectedEOF
with and without *fs.PathError.Unwrap, poll.ErrDeadlineExceeded and poll.ErrNotPollable
under *fs.PathError.Unwrap, and both "waiting for unsupported file type" entries). The
Join's operand sets are multiplied (one Wrap per combination) and the product is cut at
1024 without a marker when a callee summary is substituted
(internal/summary/eval.go, mapTreeRaw: "if len(nextCombos) == maxValues { break }").
Compare finish_join_fixpoint_limit, where one more value makes the cap visible.
-- args --
source/source.go:@seal
